    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec requires the owner response to carry a `bulkSignupWarning` flag \u2014 `true` once more than 80 owners have been created today, otherwise `false`. The acceptance test reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nI implemented it with minimal structural impact, touching **2 files** and editing **no existing method**:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `bulkSignupWarning` boolean read-only property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains `get/setBulkSignupWarning`.\n\n2. **`OwnerBulkSignupAdvice.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, cohesive `ResponseBodyAdvice` that, whenever a response body is an `OwnerDto`, sets `bulkSignupWarning = createdTodayCount() > 80`. The \"created today\" count reuses the exact same registrationDate/business-day logic already used by `OwnerDailyLimitAdvice`.\n\nThis mirrors the codebase's existing per-rule advice pattern rather than growing the already-large `OwnerRestControllerV1` (whose `addOwner`/`getOwner` methods would each pay the whole class's WMC), and the new class holds only two trivial methods so its own surrounding complexity is negligible.",
